WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.630
While fans of the new series anxiously await
"Masters of the Universe: Revelation" Part

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:10.139
2, here's a quick rundown of what the ending
of Part 1 means for the heroes and villains

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:14.170
of Eternia, and how it might lead into the
events of the second part.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:20.050
Sure, He-Man wears a hairy loincloth and Skeletor's
a wizard with a skull for a head, but they're

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.410
two of the most iconic animated characters
of the 1980s.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.200
"Masters of the Universe: Revelation" treats
them with a level of gravitas that dispels

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.690
all silliness while still staying true to
who they are.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.420
Most surprisingly, the series gets rid of
them both by the end of the first episode.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.719
Surprisingly, the pair are both vaporized
when He-Man absorbs all the magic of Eternia

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:44.960
through the Sword of Power to keep it out
of Skeletor's grasp.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.010
It's a typical heroic sacrifice, but it's
still a shock to see the series kill off its

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.679
most famous hero within the first episode.

00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:56.149
However, He-Man's death paves the way for
Teela to be thrust into the spotlight, as

00:00:56.149 --> 00:01:01.199
she renounces her new "Man at Arms" status
and goes off in exile as a mercenary.

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:07.390
But Teela eventually realizes that she has
a purpose: Alongside Orko, Andra, and Evil-Lyn,

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.670
she journeys to reunite the two blades that
make up the Sword of Power, and along the

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.210
way, she comes to understand that Eternia
and all its realms are still worth fighting

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:17.210
for.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.800
Although Teela has to grapple with the fact
that those closest to her lied about Prince

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.660
Adam's muscly He-Man alter-ego, she doesn't
let her bitterness get in the way of restoring

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.880
magic to Eternia.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.381
Yes, she has difficulty working alongside
the likes of Evil-Lyn and Beast-Man, but she

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:32.130
knows that it's all for the greater good.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.780
As the Sorceress of Castle Grayskull reveals,
Teela has to travel to the realms of Subternia

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.920
and Preternia to retrieve the two different
blades that can be reforged into the Sword

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:42.920
of Power.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.910
That's no small feat, since Subternia is a
demonic realm home to a bizarre entity known

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:52.740
as Scare Glow, which can drain any person's
life by forcing them to confront their worst

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.740
fears.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:59.090
But let's get the most pressing question out
of the way first: Is Scare Glow actually Skeletor?

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:04.010
He does have a similar skull-face, purple
cape, and armor, after all.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.150
Well, the demon has his own take on the situation,
calling himself

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.420
"The shadow of a ruler.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:16.790
Now ruler of shadows in this humble domain."

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:20.710
There's been some debate over whether Scare
Glow is Skeletor's ghost from his eventual

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:25.400
death in the future, or if he's simply a being
that Skeletor created.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:30.370
That said, a toy from 2009 lists Scare Glow's
real name as Karak Nul, and described him

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.560
as a former bounty hunter who was banished
from another dimension.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.420
Either way, Scare Glow is a formidable foe,
and his presence forces Teela to confront

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.200
her bitterness about suppressing her own heroic
status to live as a normal citizen after Prince

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.200
Adam's death.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.220
Eventually, Teela overcomes the illusion and
fights off Scare Glow by accepting her strengths,

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.400
her weaknesses, and her fear because they
all make her who she is.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.040
Giving any part of that up would be betraying
herself.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.520
Because good and evil are two sides of the
same coin, the gate to Preternia, a heavenly

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.090
realm filled with the souls of fallen heroes,
is carved into the walls of Subternia.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:11.770
Teela, Evil-Lyn, Andra, Beast-Man, and Roboto
cross over to the other side and arrive to

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.650
find none other than Prince Adam himself.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.930
It's not exactly a happy reunion for Teela,
because even though she just faced her own

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.240
inner demons in Subternia, she didn't expect
to be faced with the cause of her trust issues.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.849
Even when Prince Adam hands over the Preternian
blade, it doesn't fix things for Teela.

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:32.400
She wasn't able to mourn the loss of Prince
Adam because he was hiding a huge part of

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.780
his life from her, which she sees as a betrayal.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.770
But now that Teela has both blades, she and
Adam reforge it into the Sword of Power using

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.489
Roboto's Quark particle collider in his chest.

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:46.489
Although he already sacrificed himself to
save Eternia at the beginning of the series,

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:51.440
Prince Adam gives up his place in the paradise
to return home and restore magic to the universe,

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.450
knowing that he can never return to Preternia.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.970
In a world like Eternia, a hero always needs
a villain.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:03.080
Otherwise, he's just a do-gooder with no real
purpose -- nobody to save, and nobody to fight.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:08.099
To balance the scales of Prince Adam's resurrection,
Skeletor also makes a shocking return at the

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:13.050
end of "Masters of the Universe: Revelation"
Part 1, impaling the hero with his ram-head

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.050
staff.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:18.660
It's not the first time audiences have seen
the villain get one up on Prince Adam/He-Man,

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:24.050
but this feels pretty dire -- especially since
before this moment, it's explicitly pointed

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:29.340
out that if the titular hero dies again, he
won't return back to the Preternian paradise.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.669
But how did Skeletor make a comeback, anyway?

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:37.470
In typical villain fashion during episode
5 of "Masters of the Universe: Revelation,"

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.210
Skeletor waxes lyrical about sealing himself
inside Evil-Lyn's staff

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:49.090
"When I was to be destroyed in the orb explosion,
I was forced to seek refuge in your wand staff

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.740
to protect my essence."

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:56.590
And to add insult to injury, creator Kevin
Smith and the series' writers give Skeletor

00:04:56.590 --> 00:05:00.500
everything he's ever wanted: the Power of
Grayskull.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:05.720
Yes, that's right: It's taken just under 40
years, but the last episode of "Revelation"

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:12.150
Part 1 hands the keys over to Skeletor and
beefs him up into a hulking version of himself.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.960
It's a huge cliffhanger to leave on.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.590
It'll be interesting to see how this huge
power shift will affect the rest of Eternia

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:23.120
in Part 2, especially since reforging the
sword was meant to bring magic back into the

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.120
world.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:29.130
Will all types of sorcery and spells be warped
now that Skeletor has the power?

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.580
Only time will tell.

